      "head_commit": {
        "id": "67ed35ae672e64f7f55a7bf25f0c31c5a12fee6c",
        "tree_id": "5f0ce7ce6373ba126a3759306892520c0b2e569e",
        "message": "fix(13): find was searching an ANDROID_NDK_ROOT that does not exist\n\nTwo runs were spent on 'the NDK has no libc++_shared.so', and the NDK does have\nit. This workflow sets BOTH variables in step 5 and they disagree:\n\n    ANDROID_NDK_HOME: /home/runner/android-sdk/ndk/25.2.9519653\n    ANDROID_NDK_ROOT  -> \".../ndk/27.3.13750724\"      (does not exist)\n\nfind on a nonexistent directory prints nothing and exits 0. So the candidate loop\niterated zero times, CPP stayed empty, and the step reported the file missing --\nan accurate description of $ANDROID_NDK_ROOT and a false one about the NDK.\n\nThe NDK is now resolved by taking the first candidate that actually contains\ntoolchains/llvm/prebuilt, tried in order: ANDROID_NDK_HOME, ANDROID_NDK_ROOT,\n$ANDROID_SDK_ROOT/ndk/$NDK_VERSION, $ANDROID_HOME/ndk/$NDK_VERSION. The chosen\npath is printed, and if none matches, the step lists what IS there instead of\nasserting absence.\n\nThe recurring lesson, and it has now cost three runs in three different forms: an\nempty result from find() is not evidence of absence. A step that reports absence\nmust be the one step that proves it.\n\nAlso confirmed working in run 36443756041, before this step failed:\n    warning: gs-ffi@0.1.0: using cross-compiled llama.cpp from\n      .../native/prebuilts/android-x86_64\nGS_LLAMA_PREBUILT is set and build.rs compiles against the cross-compiled\nllama.cpp. The portable-only build is gone at build level. It remains to be\nproven by a chat() call on the device, which has still never happened.",
        "timestamp": "2026-09-28T15:56:17Z",
