        "message": "fix(12): find -type f filtered out the symlink it was looking for\n\nRun 36443756041 printed ZERO candidate lines and then:\n\n    ::error::no libc++_shared.so with Machine matching 'X86-64' under $ANDROID_NDK_ROOT\n\nimplying the NDK does not contain it. It does. -type f matches regular files\nonly, and the NDK ships libc++_shared.so as a symlink, so every candidate was\nfiltered out before the search ever looked at it. The hardcoded path for this\nsame ABI had worked on the previous run, which is what made 'it is not in the\nNDK' the wrong conclusion.\n\nDropped -type f. If it matches nothing again, the diagnostic now prints the\ncandidates it actually found rather than a bare failure.\n\nALSO CONFIRMED WORKING IN THAT RUN, before this step failed:\n\n    warning: gs-ffi@0.1.0: using cross-compiled llama.cpp from\n      .../native/prebuilts/android-x86_64\n    cargo:warning=using cross-compiled llama.cpp from ...\n\nGS_LLAMA_PREBUILT is now set and build.rs is compiling against the\ncross-compiled llama.cpp. The portable-only build is gone at build level; it\nremains to be proven by a chat() call on the device.",
